# AICL Example: Multiplayer Chess
# A two-player chess game with network support

Goal:
Create a multiplayer chess game

Constraint:
Must run on mobile devices

Constraint:
Maximum memory usage 256 MB

Constraint:
Move validation must be under 10 ms

Risk:
Server becomes unavailable

Risk:
Network latency exceeds threshold

Risk:
User disconnects unexpectedly

Risk:
Invalid move received

Recovery:
Reconnect automatically

Recovery:
Enable local mode

Recovery:
Pause game and wait for reconnection

Recovery:
Reject move and request resend

Layer:
User Interface
    Sublayer:
    Chess board rendering
    Sublayer:
    Piece animation
    Sublayer:
    Move history display
    Sublayer:
    Game status panel

Layer:
Networking
    Sublayer:
    WebSocket client
    Sublayer:
    Move synchronization
    Sublayer:
    Latency compensation

Layer:
Game Logic
    Sublayer:
    Move validation
    Sublayer:
    Check detection
    Sublayer:
    Checkmate detection
    Sublayer:
    Turn management

Layer:
Persistence
    Sublayer:
    Game state storage
    Sublayer:
    Move history

Entity Player
    name: string
    id: integer
    color: string
    rating: integer

Entity ChessPiece
    type: string
    color: string
    position: string
    has_moved: boolean

Entity GameState
    board: list
    current_turn: string
    move_count: integer
    status: string

Behavior MakeMove

Input:
    Player GameState

Output:
    GameState

Action:
    validate move and update board state

Behavior ValidateMove

Input:
    ChessPiece position

Output:
    boolean

Action:
    check if move is legal according to chess rules

Condition:

When king in check

Then highlight threatened squares

Condition:

When checkmate detected

Then end game and declare winner

Condition:

When stalemate detected

Then declare draw

Event:

On piece selection

Action:
    highlight valid moves

Event:

On move submitted

Action:
    send move to server and animate piece

Event:

On opponent move

Action:
    update board and animate opponent piece

Parallel:

User Interface
Networking

Optimize:
Move validation speed

Security:

Encrypt:
    game state

Protect:
    player credentials

Adapt:

Graphics quality

Based on:
    device performance

Validation:
Two players complete a full game

Validation:
Average latency below 100 ms

Validation:
No data loss after reconnect

Validation:
Move validation completes in under 10 ms
